[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-provider-evidence-refresh-20260908" :doc/title "Provider retention, billing and Modal evidence refresh" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "# Murakumo provider evidence refresh — 2026-09-08\n\nPrimary is Murakumo fleet. Modal is a conditional backup followed by failback to fleet. OpenRouter submission remains unsubmitted and catalog is_ready remains false.\n\n## Implemented and verified\n- API #243: seven-day content expiry now redacts request, result, partial output and error on the existing read path, including terminal jobs, at the exact deadline. Status and accounting metadata survive. 20 pure tests / 186 assertions; built API verifies create/cancel, wrong-owner denial, pre-expiry visibility, exact-boundary redaction and a fresh persisted read. This is NOT physical historical block erasure or a background sweep SLA.\n- API #244: payment replay comparison rejects changed credit recipient, amount or payment metadata with 409 idempotency-conflict. Exact duplicates retain 200; one winner gets 201. Built Worker + isolated R2 verifies 6 simultaneous identical submissions produce only one new credit; invalid billing bearer writes nothing. No real funds or customer credits were touched. This tests the existing billing service bearer, NOT OpenRouter-specific partner request credentials or token settlement.\n\n## Modal access and actual billing evidence\nThe existing junkawasakicom profile successfully accessed Modal management and billing. Earlier lack of CLI/browser login was an access-path gap, not absent credentials. Secret values were not exported or changed.\nAugust 2026 summary: metered $290.23907205; free-storage adjustment -$88.67907205; plan credits -$30; billed $171.56. This reconciles to the September 1 receipt and invoice BUMMYEHC-0010, addressed to junkawasakicom. It does not establish a registered contracting corporation.\nApp resource rows attribute $162.68110560 to murakumo-qwen38-fastmtp and $3.24297852 to murakumo-qwen38-throughput. These are historical compute/resource costs, not Qwen backup per-token rates. Resource report subtotal $199.12807420 differs from total metered cost; do not silently equate the app-resource report with the complete volume/storage bill. Free credits are not assumed permanent unit-cost reductions.\nSource email: https://mail.google.com/mail/#all/1a05d23a951923d5 . Authenticated billing exports are retained in the owner's local qualification directory, not copied into public artifacts.\n\n## Same-model backup findings\n- FastMTP app ap-6Wfsj3HcbiejMWqyC2lC5z points to the existing openai.modal.run endpoint. Its models Volume contains Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive-Q4_K_P.gguf and a matching FastMTP draft. This is not the standard b70 Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M artifact (SHA e00082f779fa385cee8c68a3ec8833a75778cc87272240b942f74e0b8243e520).\n- Throughput app ap-aiuHw8LKk1jKzXq7nhSiJg remains deployed, but its referenced model Volume vo-I5RtZRfqw9snTgUNywrIP9 returned NotFoundError through the authenticated Volume API. Its cache Volume remains readable. Deployed state is not serving-model proof.\nNo GPU container was started or model switched in this audit. A new/repaired exact-artifact backup and its auth/spend ceiling must be qualified before routing traffic. Live failover/failback and controlled restart recovery remain unmeasured.\n\n## Sustained load and measured energy\n12 rounds, 2 concurrent requests per round, 10-second pauses, synthetic long inputs and max_tokens 48; 24/24 exact-marker completions, no 429, 600.088 seconds. Successful completed output total 484 tokens. Package counter delta 14,500.999063 joules, average 24.1647876 watts. Counter is /sys/class/powercap/intel-rapl:0/energy_uj on b70 (range 65,532,610,987 microjoules); wrap handled per interval.\nThis includes pauses and any unrelated package work, excludes wall-system losses, and is not idle-subtracted. No electricity tariff, equipment amortization, network/edge allocation or attributable backup tokens have been supplied. Therefore full cost per useful token and sustainable production capacity remain unverified. This bounded test is separate from the seven-day strict-fleet observation ledger.\n\n## Remaining acceptance evidence\nPartner-scoped request authentication, stable request/attempt IDs through streaming/cancellation and invoice settlement; historical R2 deletion/GC and final retention disclosures; verified legal entity and applicable Modal Service Order; matching-model backup and stop/restart/failback; long-output continuous capacity and full operating costs.\nTargeted Gmail search for Modal service order/agreement/resale returned no matching messages; this is not proof that no contract exists. Owner clarification requested for legal name, registration/address and Modal workspace. Existing terms are at https://modal.com/legal/terms; applicability of standard restrictions and any negotiated order remains to be confirmed. No external clarification message or application was sent.\n\nEvidence hashes:\n- /Users/junkawasaki/.murakumo/openrouter-qualification/capacity-energy-1788858697866/samples.jsonl: c632791004f809ef30e45f3f8aa7f5a32a590d7046fa9af524a29991836913a3\n- /Users/junkawasaki/.murakumo/openrouter-qualification/capacity-energy-1788858697866/energy.json: 7bbcd0758d604e04d52b49de87a01aa8df5f17632f1f0cfb5693ebc8e2c5c1f1\n- /Users/junkawasaki/.murakumo/openrouter-qualification/capacity-energy-1788858697866/summary.json: 932cb73fcebd24dadd1dd2c36eead59411be00c2c5b22b7715809a1354350b11\n- /Users/junkawasaki/.murakumo/openrouter-qualification/modal-billing-202608.json: a0c167a1f340dc23ba53ac455305af04559b69d62b929eff80d967d25a2f3b86\n- /Users/junkawasaki/.murakumo/openrouter-qualification/modal-resources-202608.json: 38b718460093b4cc6a08052ccb7a680d7668c96b60c73ce9414b541f0cb8bb30\n"}]
